    'Dr. Cheikh Anta Diop (Senegal, 1923-1986) was a physicist and historian who, while Africa was still ruled from Europe, set out to show by evidence, not by myth, that ancient Egypt belonged to Africa and that Africa therefore had a history worth writing. He put the argument into Nations nègres et culture (1954), founded the radiocarbon laboratory at IFAN in Dakar, and carried it to the 1974 UNESCO symposium in Cairo, whose own report says his and Théophile Obenga’s papers were the painstakingly researched ones in the room. This lesson lets him speak, keeps the record the other side wrote, and weighs his claims by the Word.',
