    'In The African Origin of Civilization (his 1954 and 1967 chapters, in English in 1974) Diop argued that ancient Egypt was a Black African civilization, that the history of Africa cannot be written correctly until it is connected to Egypt, and that the modern West had falsified the record by inventing a foreign, white Egypt. He refused to answer the falsification with a flattering myth, and he called his readers to become research teams, not passive readers. The Word confirms the record he fought for and corrects the claims he made about the origin of the faith.',
