    'UNESCO opened its own General History of Africa volume on the ancient civilizations with Diop’s chapter, Origin of the ancient Egyptians (1981). In it he lays his evidence out line by line: humanity’s origin in Africa, the convergence of the anthropologists’ own figures, the protohistoric images, his melanin test on mummy skin, blood groups, the Greek writers, and the Egyptians’ name for themselves. He concludes that world history must be rewritten and that the truth about Africa should unite, not divide. The volume’s editor printed a note beneath it saying his arguments were not accepted by all the experts, and both the chapter and the note are the record.',
